        "title": "Your screens are ruining your posture. <em class=\"text-brand\">Slowly, but surely.</em>",
        "text": "<p>It starts with “just one more class,” “one last email,” “one more episode.” Eight hours later, your shoulders have dropped, your head is forward, and your back is taking the hit in silence.</p><p>What you’re feeling — fatigue, tension, back pain — is your body begging for a posture that no one ever taught you. The worst part? You get used to it. Until the day it becomes the norm.</p>",
        "badge": "8h / day",
        "tip": "<span class=\"font-semibold text-ink\">Every centimeter</span> your head moves forward adds up to <span class=\"font-semibold text-ink\">4 kg</span> of pressure on your cervical spine. Your back carries it for you. Every single day."
      }
